+++ b/docs/ops/observability.md
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# Observability: archive, audit and alert lanes
+
+Application logging is split into three lanes. Each lane has one job, its own
+destination and its own retention. Pick the lane before you write the line.
+
+| Lane | Purpose | Destination | Retention | Channel / call |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | Routine application logs, debug to error | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (daily rotation) | `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` (default 14) | `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (default `stack` → `daily`) |
+| **Audit** | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail | `storage/logs/audit.log` (daily rotation) | `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` (default 90) | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` |
+| **Alert** | Human-pageable ops incidents | Discord incoming webhook | Discord's own history | `app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send($title, $message, $context)` |
+
+## Archive
+
+- Default for anything a developer might want to read while debugging.
+- The `stack` channel (`LOG_STACK`, default `daily`) writes to the `daily` channel. The
+  `daily` channel honours `LOG_LEVEL` (default `debug`).
+- Expect it to be noisy. Nobody is paged by it.
+
+## Audit
+
+- Use it for facts someone may need to answer later: who did what, to whom, and when,
+  including attempts that were refused.
+- Examples: membership role changes, subscription status transitions, payment
+  refunds, login lockouts, plan-limit overrides made by an operator.
+- Write with the audit channel only:
+
+  ```php
+  Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+      'subscription_id' => $subscription->id,
+      'from' => $previous,
+      'to' => $subscription->status,
+      'actor_id' => $request->user()?->id,
+  ]);
+  ```
+
+- The audit channel's minimum level is `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` (default `info`), so `debug`
+  lines are dropped there.
+- Audit lines do **not** appear in `laravel.log`. That is intentional: the audit file is
+  the record of truth for those events, and it is kept longer.
+- Never put secrets in audit context (passwords, tokens, webhook URLs, API keys).
+
+## Alert
+
+- Use it only when a human should be woken up or must act now. It is an explicit call,
+  not a log level.
+- Examples: a job that exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook that keeps
+  failing, a plan limit that blocks an entity from working.
+- Do **not** send routine errors here. If it is only useful when you are already
+  reading logs, it belongs in the archive.
+- Call `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send()` with a short title, a message and a small
+  context array:
+
+  ```php
+  app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+      'Asaas webhook failing',
+      'Webhook processing failed after retries',
+      ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks', 'entity_id' => $entity->id],
+  );
+  ```
+
+- The webhook URL comes from `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`. When it is empty the call is a
+  no-op, so local and test environments send nothing.
+- Keep the text short. It is truncated to 1800 characters.
+- Redaction is automatic. Context keys that look sensitive (`password`, `token`,
+  `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook`) are replaced with
+  `[redacted]`, as are strings containing a `Bearer` credential. Do not rely on it as a
+  reason to pass secrets; leave them out.
+- Delivery is best effort. A non-2xx answer or a transport error is written to the
+  archive as an `error` line ("Discord ops alert failed") and never thrown to the caller.
+- The notifier is wired into nothing yet. Each call site is a deliberate decision.
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. Would a person want to be woken up or act now if this happened? → **Alert** (and
+   also keep the normal error log, if any).
+2. Is it a fact about who changed or attempted something that must survive for
+   later review? → **Audit**.
+3. Otherwise → **Archive** (`Log::...`).
+
+If you are unsure between archive and audit, ask: "Would an auditor expect this to
+exist in 90 days?" If yes, it is audit. Audit does not replace the archive for
+debugging, so an event that matters for both can be written to both.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Env key | Default | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels behind the default `stack` channel. |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Minimum level for the archive channels. |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level for the audit channel. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days. |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | *(empty)* | Empty disables alerts. Treat as a secret. |
+
+There is deliberately no `discord` log channel. Discord is reached only through
+`DiscordOpsAlert`, never through `Log::`.
+
+See also [`devops.md`](devops.md) for the deployment and environment layout.
